# The image is a bot that reads two directories and holds one connection open. Everything
# below is either useless to it or grows without bound, and a container image is the wrong
# place for either.

.git
.github
.venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.env
.env.example

# The pipeline's working set. `data/events` alone reaches roughly 90 MB a year and the bot
# never opens it: `/latest` renders a stored briefing and `/status` folds the run history,
# so `data/briefings` and `data/runs` are the whole of what it needs.
#
# Named individually rather than excluding `data` and re-admitting two children. The
# re-inclusion form reads better and depends on how a builder resolves an exception under
# an excluded parent, which is not the same everywhere; a build that silently ships 90 MB,
# or one that fails on a missing COPY, is not worth the tidier file.
data/articles
data/events
data/ai-pulse.log
data/state.json

site
tests
evals
scripts
docs
PLAN.md
TODO.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
requirements.lock
